KNOWNBUG with the headers of libstdc++ 16 (gcc 16) only; passes with gcc 11-15
headers.  Reproduce by preprocessing with g++-16 -E (the predefined macros
select the code paths) and running cbmc on the .ii file.
Also: no body for std::ctype<wchar_t>::do_widen/do_toupper/do_tolower and
ctype<char>::_M_widen_init with gcc 16 (the wchar_t facet is reached).
2026-09-25: the CONVERSION ERROR is gone -- it was __gnu_cxx::__atomic_add's
__atomic_fetch_add (GCC atomic builtins were unusable in C++); the user
assertion is SUCCESS.  Remaining: "no body for callee
std::ctype<wchar_t>::do_widen/do_toupper/do_tolower" (the wchar_t facet's
virtuals) -> VERIFICATION FAILED.  A header-free reduction of the
remaining part is in progress (/tmp/r160/red).
2026-09-30 (round 163m): passes.  The modelled "C" locale ctype<char> facet
(cpp_typecheck_stdlib.cpp) now also fills the _M_widen / _M_narrow caches
with the identity and sets _M_widen_ok / _M_narrow_ok
([facet.ctype.char.virtuals]/1, [facet.ctype.virtuals]/11), so
ctype<char>::widen needs no virtual call on the modelled object.  Checked
by preprocessing in archlinux (GCC 16.2.1); a WRONG assertion was added, and any other failed property (the facet's
pointer checks and missing bodies on bin53) is forbidden.
